meta {
  name: Size of downloading a collection (symbols x intervals x days)
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/collections/:name/estimate?intervals=<intervals>&days=1
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  intervals: <intervals>
  days: 1
  ~allowStale: true
}

params:path {
  name: large-caps
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{apiKey}}
}

docs {
  Size of downloading a collection (symbols x intervals x days)

  - An API key with the `read` scope (any key).

  Rows, bytes and broker calls before you start. An option universe is resolved first (a stale price is accepted for a
  count and is labelled in `atmSource`). An estimate: a recently listed contract has fewer days than asked, and a broker
  may keep less intraday history than you ask for.

  Reference: docs/api/collections/estimateCollection.md in the repository.
}
